WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.466 --> 00:00:06.133
Hi there. And welcome. I’m Professor Sycamore.

2
00:00:06.199 --> 00:00:08.033
As a Pokémon researcher,

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.166
I work with Trainers in the Kalos region to help them with their journey.

4
00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:15.366
It’s time for my annual Pokémon summer camp,

5
00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:20.366
where together, you and your Pokémon can create marvelous memories.

6
00:00:22.666 --> 00:00:27.700
- Wow. There it is.
- Pika, Pika!

7
00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:37.400
- The beach.
- So pretty.

8
00:00:37.466 --> 00:00:41.633
I love that smell. Ocean air.

9
00:00:41.699 --> 00:00:43.933
- Professor Sycamore.
- Pika!

10
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.766
- Hi! Hi.
- Long-time no see.

11
00:00:46.833 --> 00:00:49.933
- Hi there!
- It was so nice of you to invite us.

12
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.733
In the midst of our heroes’ journey to Shalour City,

13
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.566
Professor Sycamore has invited them

14
00:00:55.633 --> 00:00:58.766
to be part of his annual Pokémon summer camp.

15
00:01:00.066 --> 00:01:02.833
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

16
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.566
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

17
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.300
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

18
00:01:09.366 --> 00:01:12.300
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

19
00:01:12.366 --> 00:01:15.133
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

20
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.566
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

21
00:01:18.633 --> 00:01:22.000
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

22
00:01:22.066 --> 00:01:24.433
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

23
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.933
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

24
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.000
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

25
00:01:44.333 --> 00:01:47.233
As we thought, the twerps did make the scene.

26
00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.800
We hit that on the head.

27
00:01:48.866 --> 00:01:52.000
With the professor as host, their appearance was a must.

28
00:01:52.066 --> 00:01:53.566
Let’s take it slow.

29
00:01:53.633 --> 00:01:57.633
And at the right time, we’ll whisk all their Pokémon away in one fell swoop.

30
00:01:57.699 --> 00:02:00.600
Working to earn everyone’s trust is a must.

31
00:02:00.666 --> 00:02:02.966
- You.
- Huh?

32
00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:05.966
Uh, Madame Catherine. You’re right on time.

33
00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:09.166
We’re just getting our gourmet preparations underway now.

34
00:02:09.233 --> 00:02:11.466
Good. No skimping, please.

35
00:02:11.533 --> 00:02:16.033
Keep in mind Augustine’s Trainers have giant appetites and just love to eat.

36
00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.400
Prepare a ton of food at least.

37
00:02:18.466 --> 00:02:19.900
Yes, ma’am.

38
00:02:19.966 --> 00:02:22.266
And if they really like what you all cook,

39
00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:25.133
there might just be a little raise in store.

40
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.633
Huh! Yummy!

41
00:02:28.633 --> 00:02:31.466
- And that’s what happened.
- Mm.

42
00:02:31.533 --> 00:02:37.233
Wow. Great. What a marvelous experience. You met Mega Lucario.

43
00:02:37.299 --> 00:02:39.866
Mega Evolution is as cool as it gets.

44
00:02:39.933 --> 00:02:43.633
Everything powers up, including the strength of their moves.

45
00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.500
It’s awesome how strong they get.

46
00:02:45.566 --> 00:02:50.266
I wish I could have seen it, too, so I guess, you’ll be battling Korrina

47
00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:53.666
and that powerful Mega Lucario at the Shalour Gym soon.

48
00:02:53.733 --> 00:02:57.833
You bet! The stronger my opponent is, the more fired up I get.

49
00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.966
- I’m going to win that Gym badge for sure.
- Pika!

50
00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:05.133
Well, I hope your stay here will be useful and marvelous at the same time.

51
00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.533
Thanks.

52
00:03:08.233 --> 00:03:10.833
This is the cabin you’ll be staying in.

53
00:03:10.899 --> 00:03:13.500
Mm, it’s the cutest!

54
00:03:13.566 --> 00:03:15.799
Everyone will be split into teams.

55
00:03:15.866 --> 00:03:19.000
As you can see, your team is called Team Froakie.

56
00:03:19.066 --> 00:03:21.566
Team Froakie, huh? Cool.

57
00:03:26.799 --> 00:03:29.466
- Okay, I call this bed!
- Na-na-na!

58
00:03:32.466 --> 00:03:33.966
Oh!

59
00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:35.966
Speaking of summer camp,

60
00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:39.933
does this bring back any memories of when you two first met each other?

61
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.433
- Yeah, it does.
- Huh?

62
00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.733
Let’s make it as much fun as when we were kids.

63
00:03:43.799 --> 00:03:45.066
It’s a deal.

64
00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:46.933
- All right, battle begin.
- Huh?

65
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.100
-Squirt!

66
00:03:49.166 --> 00:03:51.166
Hey, it’s a Squirtle.

67
00:03:51.233 --> 00:03:53.033
Huh?

68
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.466
Squirtle. The Tiny Turtle Pokémon.

69
00:03:57.533 --> 00:04:00.066
During battle, Squirtle hides in its shell,

70
00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:02.733
then it sprays water at its opponent whenever it can.

71
00:04:02.799 --> 00:04:06.333
Conkeldurr, Superpower!

72
00:04:06.399 --> 00:04:08.733
Quick, Squirtle. Dodge by getting in close.

73
00:04:13.066 --> 00:04:16.733
- Whoa, it jumped!
- Yeah and it jumped high!

74
00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.466
- Squirtle!
- Conkeldurr!

75
00:04:22.866 --> 00:04:24.300
Hey. Stop moving!

76
00:04:24.366 --> 00:04:27.500
But it’s what we do. We just can’t stand still. See?

77
00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:30.266
Squirtle!

78
00:04:30.333 --> 00:04:32.400
Wow, it’s as if they’re dancing.

79
00:04:32.466 --> 00:04:34.933
- That Squirtle’s something else.
- Pika!

80
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.700
It’s having lots of fun battling.

81
00:04:36.766 --> 00:04:38.933
You’re right. Look at that smile!

82
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.800
- Squirtle!
- Now Skull Bash.

83
00:04:41.866 --> 00:04:43.833
Squirtle!

84
00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:48.666
Keldurr!

85
00:04:48.733 --> 00:04:51.166
- Conkeldurr!
- We nailed that one.

86
00:04:51.233 --> 00:04:54.500
- Ha, Squirtle wins it.
- Squirtle!

87
00:04:57.433 --> 00:05:00.633
Thanks, Conkeldurr. Good job.

88
00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.666
Boy, oh boy. Your battle style's a first for me.

89
00:05:03.733 --> 00:05:07.266
We love to dance. We just keep on moving and grooving.

90
00:05:07.333 --> 00:05:10.933
- Hey. Can I battle with you next?
- Pika! Pika!

91
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.766
All right. Sounds great.

92
00:05:12.833 --> 00:05:15.433
I’m Tierno and I’m from Santalune City.

93
00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.633
- And Squirtle here’s my partner.
- Squirtle!

94
00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:21.466
We’re part of Team Squirtle. What about you guys?

95
00:05:21.533 --> 00:05:26.200
All of us are part of Team Froakie. I’m Ash Ketchum. I’m from Pallet Town.

96
00:05:26.266 --> 00:05:28.500
- My partner’s Pikachu.
- Pikachu!

97
00:05:28.566 --> 00:05:31.099
- Huh? Pallet Town?
- That’s right.

98
00:05:31.166 --> 00:05:35.000
See, I’m from Kanto, but I came here so I can enter the Kalos League.

99
00:05:35.066 --> 00:05:37.733
Some haul. All the way from Kanto, huh?

100
00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:42.000
- Hold on. I know you.
- Huh? Wait. You do?

101
00:05:42.066 --> 00:05:43.800
Yeah. Stay here!

102
00:05:43.866 --> 00:05:45.233
- Now what?
- Pika?

103
00:05:48.066 --> 00:05:50.233
Look. Check it out. She looks the same.

104
00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:54.133
It’s you. This is great. You’re Serena.

105
00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.633
But how could you know my name?

106
00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:00.233
- Because I saw you on PokéVision.
- Huh?

107
00:06:03.433 --> 00:06:06.566
- Wait. Isn’t PokéVision--
- Pika?

108
00:06:06.633 --> 00:06:08.599
Yup. Remember Serena’s video?

109
00:06:08.666 --> 00:06:14.700
Oh, no! That means people are watching me, too?

110
00:06:14.766 --> 00:06:18.133
Course they are. Come on. That’s the whole point, silly!

111
00:06:19.466 --> 00:06:23.333
- I’m Shauna. Nice to meet you.
- Shauna. Thank you.

112
00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.566
You and Fennekin are so cute in your video

113
00:06:25.633 --> 00:06:28.099
that I’ve been a fan ever since I first saw it.

114
00:06:28.166 --> 00:06:29.833
Oh, wow! Thanks.

115
00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:33.266
- Where’d you see the video?
- Where? At the Pokémon Center.

116
00:06:33.333 --> 00:06:36.599
You can watch it anywhere. You haven’t seen your video yet?

117
00:06:36.666 --> 00:06:37.900
Uh...

118
00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:43.233
Your Squirtle is just fine and back to perfect health.

119
00:06:43.299 --> 00:06:45.299
- Thanks, Nurse Joy.
- Squirtle!

120
00:06:45.366 --> 00:06:48.233
Glad you’re feeling good, kiddo.

121
00:06:49.666 --> 00:06:52.266
Whenever I visit the Pokémon Center,

122
00:06:52.333 --> 00:06:55.166
I always check if something’s new on PokéVision.

123
00:06:55.233 --> 00:06:59.033
See? This one is Serena’s. Look how many views it’s gotten.

124
00:06:59.099 --> 00:07:02.400
That’s great! I had no idea they were watching.

125
00:07:02.466 --> 00:07:05.833
- Can I meet your Fennekin, please?
- Sure, no problem.

126
00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:09.799
Fennekin, come on out.

127
00:07:09.866 --> 00:07:11.033
Fennekin!

128
00:07:11.099 --> 00:07:15.866
So cute. You’re too cute. Fennekin’s even cuter in person.

129
00:07:15.933 --> 00:07:17.599
Thank you, Shauna.

130
00:07:17.666 --> 00:07:22.733
Grooming its tail must be lots of work, but it’s so totally shiny and smooth.

131
00:07:22.799 --> 00:07:26.166
That’s so sweet. It’s because I brush it all the time.

132
00:07:26.233 --> 00:07:28.533
Do you make PokéVision videos too?

133
00:07:28.599 --> 00:07:30.900
Sure do. I’ve made a whole bunch.

134
00:07:32.366 --> 00:07:34.066
Whoa, that’s a lot.

135
00:07:34.133 --> 00:07:36.666
- Huh!
- I make one when I catch a new Pokémon.

136
00:07:36.733 --> 00:07:38.500
I even make a new video every time

137
00:07:38.566 --> 00:07:41.033
I manage to get my hands on a pretty new ribbon.

138
00:07:43.966 --> 00:07:45.766
Bulbasaur!

139
00:07:45.833 --> 00:07:51.200
Time for Shauna’s Pokémon Show. My partner for today is Bulbasaur.

140
00:07:51.266 --> 00:07:52.933
It’s super cute when it runs

141
00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.133
and even with its short legs, Bulbasaur’s really good at running.

142
00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:59.799
- It was my very first Pokémon.
- Bulbasaur!

143
00:07:59.866 --> 00:08:03.266
Everybody’s favorite.

144
00:08:03.333 --> 00:08:06.633
- It has a super-cute voice too.
- Bulba!

145
00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:09.233
Can’t wait to see what will bloom from its seed.

146
00:08:09.299 --> 00:08:11.766
I hope that you’re all excited, too.

147
00:08:14.766 --> 00:08:16.400
Well, there it is.

148
00:08:16.466 --> 00:08:20.433
- You’ve got a Bulbasaur.
- Yup. It’s my go-to Pokémon pal.

149
00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:23.500
Bulbasaur, come out.

150
00:08:24.933 --> 00:08:26.166
Bulbasaur!

151
00:08:26.233 --> 00:08:29.166
-Just like in the video.

152
00:08:30.466 --> 00:08:32.766
Bulbasaur, the Seed Pokémon.

153
00:08:32.833 --> 00:08:35.533
A young Bulbasaur uses the nutrients from its seed

154
00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:37.333
for the energy it needs to grow.

155
00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:39.866
Don’t you think Bulbasaur’s super-cute too?

156
00:08:39.933 --> 00:08:44.033
- Sure do.
- Squirt! Squirto! Squirt?

157
00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:46.633
- Pika!
- Fenn!

158
00:08:46.699 --> 00:08:47.866
Saur!

159
00:08:49.833 --> 00:08:52.866
I guess your Bulbasaur’s kind of snooty, huh?

160
00:08:52.933 --> 00:08:55.300
- Yeah.
- Huh?

161
00:08:55.366 --> 00:08:56.733
Chespin!

162
00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.133
- Chespin.
- I think Chespin wants to play.

163
00:09:00.199 --> 00:09:02.500
Froakie, come on out.

164
00:09:03.566 --> 00:09:06.800
Froakie!

165
00:09:06.866 --> 00:09:09.166
- Oh yeah.
- Huh?

166
00:09:09.233 --> 00:09:11.133
Ta-da!

167
00:09:11.199 --> 00:09:14.433
- Poké Puffs. Did you bake these, Serena?
- Mm-hm.

168
00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:19.133
Here. I hope you all like them. For you.

169
00:09:19.199 --> 00:09:22.699
Squirto! Squirt!

170
00:09:22.766 --> 00:09:25.166
- Well?
- Squirto!

171
00:09:28.766 --> 00:09:30.466
Bulbasaur, one for you?

172
00:09:30.533 --> 00:09:33.233
- Saur!
- Huh?

173
00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:36.800
Sorry. Because my Bulbasaur’s a teensy bit shy around others,

174
00:09:36.866 --> 00:09:39.000
it won’t eat anything unless I feed it.

175
00:09:39.066 --> 00:09:40.699
- Then go right ahead.
- Thanks.

176
00:09:42.699 --> 00:09:44.199
Here. It’s for you.

177
00:09:45.866 --> 00:09:50.133
Bulbasaur. Saur. Saur!

178
00:09:50.199 --> 00:09:52.033
Huh? Was that a smile?

179
00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:54.100
-Bulbasaur really loves it.

180
00:09:54.166 --> 00:09:56.466
But that’s the most emotion you’ll ever see.

181
00:09:56.533 --> 00:09:58.500
I’m so glad you like my Poké Puffs.

182
00:09:58.566 --> 00:10:02.166
Char! Char! Char!

183
00:10:02.233 --> 00:10:03.866
-Pika?

184
00:10:03.933 --> 00:10:05.433
Wow. Charmander.

185
00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.000
Charmander! Char!

186
00:10:08.066 --> 00:10:11.033
Who’s that Pokémon?

187
00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.100
It’s Squirtle.

188
00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:27.033
- Wow. Energetic!
- So that’s a Charmander.

189
00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.900
Charmander, the Lizard Pokémon.

190
00:10:30.966 --> 00:10:33.566
When the tip of Charmander’s tail burns brightly,

191
00:10:33.633 --> 00:10:36.233
that indicates it’s in good health.

192
00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:37.699
Char!

193
00:10:37.766 --> 00:10:41.333
All three of the Kanto Pokémon new Trainers choose from are here.

194
00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:44.766
- Where’s Charmander’s Trainer?
- Right there. That’s him.

195
00:10:46.433 --> 00:10:50.500
- Hey, it’s Trevs.
- I made it.

196
00:10:50.566 --> 00:10:53.733
- Trevor, you’re so late.
- Sorry.

197
00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:56.800
You see, Charmander was at it again on our way here.

198
00:10:56.866 --> 00:10:58.233
Again?

199
00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:01.300
What do you mean? Charmander was at what again?

200
00:11:01.366 --> 00:11:03.699
All right. The thing is… Huh?

201
00:11:03.766 --> 00:11:06.366
Charmander!

202
00:11:07.366 --> 00:11:11.199
- Che! Che! Che! Che! Che!
- Squirto!

203
00:11:12.166 --> 00:11:14.699
Well, Charmander’s always ready to battle.

204
00:11:14.766 --> 00:11:18.133
I’m so sorry for Charmander’s actions towards your Pokémon.

205
00:11:18.199 --> 00:11:21.699
It doesn’t matter where it is. Charmander’s always so full of energy.

206
00:11:21.766 --> 00:11:23.833
It got into a fight on the way here, right?

207
00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:25.433
Charmander!

208
00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:29.733
This is Trevor. The three of us have been friends since we were little.

209
00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:33.400
How are you? I’m really sorry about all this.

210
00:11:33.466 --> 00:11:36.133
Huh? It can’t be. You’re Serena!

211
00:11:36.199 --> 00:11:37.199
Huh?

212
00:11:37.266 --> 00:11:40.133
It’s Poké Vision! That video made you famous.

213
00:11:40.199 --> 00:11:43.699
Shauna kept saying how there’s this really pretty girl on a video.

214
00:11:43.766 --> 00:11:46.133
She must have showed it to me a million times.

215
00:11:46.199 --> 00:11:50.133
Huh! Uh, heh, I’m a little embarrassed.

216
00:11:50.199 --> 00:11:53.333
Wow. You’re just so cute.

217
00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:56.133
Don’t mind him. He’s a goofball.

218
00:11:56.199 --> 00:11:59.633
- Are you Pikachu?
- Pika.

219
00:12:02.433 --> 00:12:03.633
Uh...

220
00:12:03.699 --> 00:12:06.766
I like to take photos of all the Pokémon I’ve met.

221
00:12:11.666 --> 00:12:15.333
My dream is to meet every Pokémon listed in the Pokédex

222
00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:19.500
and someday discover a new Pokémon that hasn’t even been listed yet.

223
00:12:19.566 --> 00:12:20.866
That sounds great.

224
00:12:20.933 --> 00:12:23.833
This is Ash, Serena, Bonnie and Clemont.

225
00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:26.500
Ash came all the way from the Kanto region.

226
00:12:26.566 --> 00:12:29.733
Then that means you’ve come across a bunch of Pokémon from Kanto

227
00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:33.066
that I haven’t ever seen before. I’m so jealous.

228
00:12:33.133 --> 00:12:35.199
So, are all of you staying for camp?

229
00:12:35.266 --> 00:12:37.566
Uh-huh. We’re part of Team Froakie.

230
00:12:37.633 --> 00:12:39.933
All four of us are traveling together.

231
00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:42.599
Big group. Must be a lot of fun.

232
00:12:42.666 --> 00:12:44.666
You guys don’t travel together?

233
00:12:44.733 --> 00:12:48.733
The three of us got our Pokémon from Professor Sycamore on the same day,

234
00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:51.933
but went our separate ways to pursue our dreams.

235
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.599
Oh, I see.

236
00:12:53.666 --> 00:12:55.833
But every now and then, we like to get together

237
00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.900
and catch up on what everyone’s been up to.

238
00:12:57.966 --> 00:12:59.066
- Chespin! Che!
- Cha!

239
00:12:59.133 --> 00:13:01.133
Why are you on a journey, Ash?

240
00:13:01.199 --> 00:13:04.733
That’s easy. I started traveling so I can become a Pokémon Master.

241
00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.033
Pi! Pika!

242
00:13:06.099 --> 00:13:08.866
So becoming a Pokémon Master’s your dream, huh?

243
00:13:08.933 --> 00:13:10.933
Sure is.

244
00:13:12.166 --> 00:13:15.300
All right, it’s time to gather on the beach for introductions,

245
00:13:15.366 --> 00:13:18.066
as the Pokémon summer camp gets under way.

246
00:13:18.133 --> 00:13:20.333
- Come on, let’s hurry!
- All right!

247
00:13:23.699 --> 00:13:26.000
Dreams, huh?

248
00:13:26.066 --> 00:13:28.366
- What’s wrong, Serena?
- Huh?

249
00:13:28.433 --> 00:13:31.733
Nothing. I’m coming.

250
00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:35.466
Hello, Trainers. Thank you all for being here.

251
00:13:35.533 --> 00:13:37.000
And why are you here?

252
00:13:37.066 --> 00:13:40.199
You’re here to build an even deeper bond with your Pokémon

253
00:13:40.266 --> 00:13:42.433
through your interactions with other Trainers.

254
00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.666
Starting today and throughout the week,

255
00:13:44.733 --> 00:13:48.166
I hope you’ll have lots of summer camp fun.

256
00:13:48.233 --> 00:13:50.699
And now, presenting Nurse Joy!

257
00:13:50.766 --> 00:13:53.166
She’s opened a Pokémon Center just for us.

258
00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:57.533
I’m happy to care for your Pokémon anytime you need me.

259
00:13:57.599 --> 00:13:58.666
Wigglytuff!

260
00:13:58.733 --> 00:14:00.800
And here’s our food service manager,

261
00:14:00.866 --> 00:14:04.733
who takes good care of us every year, Madame Catherine.

262
00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:09.233
My job is to make certain you have the most delicious meals all week long.

263
00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:13.133
Of course, I have three excellent chefs to help me. The best.

264
00:14:13.199 --> 00:14:15.233
Hi-ho, campers!

265
00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:19.400
All right. At our camp, we have a system where each team earns points,

266
00:14:19.466 --> 00:14:22.133
depending on how they did in each day’s activities.

267
00:14:22.199 --> 00:14:24.300
- Let’s have fun.
- Right.

268
00:14:24.366 --> 00:14:26.666
Okay, Team Froakie, let’s go!

269
00:14:26.733 --> 00:14:30.266
Ready, Team Squirtle? Let’s do it with style.

270
00:14:30.333 --> 00:14:31.933
- Right.
- We’ll do our best.

271
00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:35.800
First place gets ten points. Second place gets seven points.

272
00:14:35.866 --> 00:14:38.033
Third place gets three points.

273
00:14:38.099 --> 00:14:40.566
And all other teams get no points.

274
00:14:40.633 --> 00:14:43.433
The goal is to help each other out while competing.

275
00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:46.433
The team that has earned the most points by the last day

276
00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:51.433
will have the honor of being inducted into the Pokémon summer camp hall of fame.

277
00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.699
Also, please note the current Champion Diantha

278
00:14:54.766 --> 00:14:59.366
was inducted into the summer camp hall of fame back when she was your age.

279
00:14:59.433 --> 00:15:01.400
- That’s so cool.
- Wow!

280
00:15:01.466 --> 00:15:05.333
And that means we’ll be able to follow in the footsteps of the great Diantha.

281
00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:07.199
I want to do what she did!

282
00:15:07.266 --> 00:15:11.199
- Yeah, Pikachu, let’s go for it.
- Pika! Pika!

283
00:15:11.266 --> 00:15:14.400
Now, on our first day, we like to get everyone acquainted

284
00:15:14.466 --> 00:15:16.566
by starting off with a Pokémon battle.

285
00:15:16.633 --> 00:15:19.166
It’s an annual tradition where no points are awarded,

286
00:15:19.233 --> 00:15:22.066
so feel free to challenge any Trainer you like.

287
00:15:22.133 --> 00:15:24.333
I want my opponent to be Tierno.

288
00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:27.300
- We’ll battle for sure this time.
- All right.

289
00:15:27.366 --> 00:15:30.300
- Serena, what do you say?
- Hm!

290
00:15:30.366 --> 00:15:32.833
So that means I’ll be your opponent.

291
00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:35.033
And may the best Trainer win!

292
00:15:36.366 --> 00:15:38.466
Is everybody ready?

293
00:15:39.699 --> 00:15:41.233
Battles begin!

294
00:15:53.166 --> 00:15:55.166
- Ready, Froakie?
- Kie!

295
00:15:55.233 --> 00:15:57.766
Pikachu, cheer us on with Bonnie, all right?

296
00:15:57.833 --> 00:15:59.833
- Pika!
- You can do it, Ash!

297
00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:02.400
You’re using Froakie, not Pikachu?

298
00:16:02.466 --> 00:16:06.400
I got Froakie from Professor Sycamore when I first got to the Kalos region.

299
00:16:06.466 --> 00:16:09.066
All right, a Water-type battle.

300
00:16:09.133 --> 00:16:11.900
There’s no doubt we both want to get into the hall of fame.

301
00:16:11.966 --> 00:16:14.400
Yup. There’s no holding back.

302
00:16:14.466 --> 00:16:17.766
Let’s win this with style.

303
00:16:17.833 --> 00:16:19.133
Bulba! Bulba!

304
00:16:19.199 --> 00:16:21.066
-Fennekin!

305
00:16:21.133 --> 00:16:25.000
- Hey, you could be a bit more excited.
- Huh?

306
00:16:25.066 --> 00:16:28.400
You see, this is the first time I’m competing in an official battle

307
00:16:28.466 --> 00:16:30.733
- with a real judge.
- Fennekin!

308
00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:33.333
Huh, even though you’re a Trainer?

309
00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:34.933
Yeah. This is it.

310
00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:38.966
Amazing. That means today is your official debut Pokémon battle!

311
00:16:39.033 --> 00:16:41.366
You’re right. I guess it is!

312
00:16:41.433 --> 00:16:45.466
- Let’s do our best, Fennekin!
- Kin! Fenn!

313
00:16:45.533 --> 00:16:48.966
- Charmander. Let’s really focus, okay?
- Charmander!

314
00:16:49.033 --> 00:16:51.733
Chespin. We’ve got to win this, all right?

315
00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:53.199
Chespin!

316
00:16:53.266 --> 00:16:55.966
- Would you look at that?
- Pokémon aplenty.

317
00:16:56.033 --> 00:16:57.566
Yup. Stealer’s choice.

318
00:16:57.633 --> 00:16:59.033
Rejoice!

319
00:16:59.099 --> 00:17:02.666
Excuse me, but there’s a dinner that’s begging to be prepared, right?

320
00:17:02.733 --> 00:17:04.233
Right!

321
00:17:08.466 --> 00:17:11.966
Fennekin, use Flamethrower. Fenn!

322
00:17:12.033 --> 00:17:14.200
Use Energy Ball!

323
00:17:16.733 --> 00:17:18.233
Fenn!

324
00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:21.166
- Fennekin, are you okay?
- Fennekin!

325
00:17:21.233 --> 00:17:25.333
What power. Despite it not being very effective against Fire types.

326
00:17:25.399 --> 00:17:29.200
See? And cute too. That’s power with style.

327
00:17:29.266 --> 00:17:33.066
My dream is to one day become the world’s greatest Pokémon performer.

328
00:17:33.133 --> 00:17:35.800
- World’s greatest Pokémon performer?
- Fennekin?

329
00:17:35.866 --> 00:17:38.133
Wow, you’ve never heard of them? They’re Trainers

330
00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:41.466
who create high-quality performances working together with their Pokémon.

331
00:17:41.533 --> 00:17:44.533
-Dodge it, quick.

332
00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:47.600
Che!

333
00:17:47.666 --> 00:17:49.966
Che? Che! Che! Che! Che!

334
00:17:50.033 --> 00:17:55.700
Chespin. Calm down, please. Come on, calm down.

335
00:17:56.933 --> 00:18:01.100
Please excuse us. Chespin, can you still battle?

336
00:18:01.166 --> 00:18:03.166
Ches! Che!

337
00:18:03.233 --> 00:18:05.333
Kie!

338
00:18:05.399 --> 00:18:08.566
- How does it do that?
- It’s the rhythm.

339
00:18:08.633 --> 00:18:10.466
- The rhythm?
- Word up.

340
00:18:10.533 --> 00:18:13.666
My dream is for my Pokémon and I to be a rad dance team.

341
00:18:13.733 --> 00:18:14.933
Sounds awesome.

342
00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:18.500
You bet. We’re using rhythm and dance steps while we’re battling.

343
00:18:18.566 --> 00:18:21.933
Dodging is a breeze when you’re able to move and groove like us.

344
00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:24.533
Okay, Rapid Spin. Let’s go!

345
00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:26.433
Squirtle!

346
00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:31.700
- Froakie, Water Pulse again.
- Fro! Kie?

347
00:18:31.766 --> 00:18:34.066
All right. This battle's over.

348
00:18:34.133 --> 00:18:37.433
I’m going to stop the battle, which means Squirtle is the winner.

349
00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:40.399
Squirtle! Squirtle!

350
00:18:40.466 --> 00:18:44.000
Pretty cool, huh? Looks like we’ll be getting into the hall of fame.

351
00:18:45.766 --> 00:18:48.000
Wow! You two can really move.

352
00:18:48.066 --> 00:18:52.000
Squirtle! Squirtle! Squirtle! Squirtle! Squirtle! Squirtle! Squirtle! Squirtle!

353
00:18:52.066 --> 00:18:54.066
Fro.

354
00:18:55.266 --> 00:18:57.566
You never know what Ash is going to do.

355
00:18:57.633 --> 00:19:01.000
I’m always learning new things to do for Pokémon through his actions.

356
00:19:01.066 --> 00:19:02.866
You’re never sure of what’s next.

357
00:19:02.933 --> 00:19:06.300
Oh, man, come on! It’s not such a big deal.

358
00:19:06.366 --> 00:19:08.433
But your inventions are totally amazing.

359
00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:12.266
- An inventor?
- His inventions are always helping us out.

360
00:19:12.333 --> 00:19:14.566
Here.

361
00:19:14.633 --> 00:19:16.700
- Huh?
- Whoa! What’s that?

362
00:19:16.766 --> 00:19:18.766
Inventing is my passion.

363
00:19:18.833 --> 00:19:21.966
I love coming up with things that benefit the lives of Pokémon.

364
00:19:22.033 --> 00:19:24.500
My brother’s inventions are unbelievable.

365
00:19:24.566 --> 00:19:27.433
Awesome. That’s so cool.

366
00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:30.666
Serena, how did your battle against Shauna go?

367
00:19:30.733 --> 00:19:34.166
It was a lot of fun. I figured out a lot of things.

368
00:19:34.233 --> 00:19:38.166
Shauna showed me a lot of things too.

369
00:19:41.633 --> 00:19:43.633
They seem to enjoy our cuisine.

370
00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.733
It’s all because of your recipes.

371
00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:48.333
It’s all because I’m the official taste tester.

372
00:19:48.399 --> 00:19:50.233
Wait. You can’t brag about that!

373
00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:51.800
- Wobbuffet!
- Huh?

374
00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:59.033
You’ve done a great job!

375
00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:02.200
The kids just adore your cooking. Raise time.

376
00:20:02.266 --> 00:20:04.366
Huh, thanks!

377
00:20:13.866 --> 00:20:17.200
- Becoming a Pokémon Master.
- Fenn?

378
00:20:17.266 --> 00:20:19.266
Ash isn’t the only one.

379
00:20:19.333 --> 00:20:23.000
There’s Clemont, Shauna, Tierno and Trevor.

380
00:20:23.066 --> 00:20:26.166
They’re all on a journey to make their dreams come true.

381
00:20:26.233 --> 00:20:27.733
Fenn!

382
00:20:29.533 --> 00:20:31.833
But I need a dream, too.

383
00:20:33.866 --> 00:20:38.266
Day one of Professor Sycamore’s Pokémon summer camp is almost at an end.

384
00:20:38.333 --> 00:20:41.700
With so many new friends and experiences to reflect upon,

385
00:20:41.766 --> 00:20:48.399
only time will tell if it will affect our heroes, as the journey continues.
